# Double division with integer operands

Divides 7 by 2.25 in both operand orders to verify the integer is
promoted and the result keeps full double-precision representation,
producing 3.111111111111111 and 0.32142857142857145.

>>> source
integer_left: int = 7
double_value: double = 2.25

// Verifies the Int-to-Double promotion. The f64 result carries the expected
// double-precision representation.
integer_divided_by_double: double = integer_left / double_value
print(integer_divided_by_double)

// Verifies the same promotion with the operand order reversed.
double_divided_by_integer: double = double_value / integer_left
print(double_divided_by_integer)

<<< stdout
3.111111111111111
0.32142857142857145

<<< stderr
